<title>GERMANY: NRW March CPI falls 0.2 pct, up 1.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>NRW March CPI falls 0.2 pct, up 1.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The statistics Office in the west German state of North Rhine-Westphalia said on Monday that the cost of living fell 0.2 percent in March from February. Compared with March 1996, the cost of living rose by 1.8 percent.</p>
<p>In February, the state reported an 0.5 percent rise month-on-month and a 2.0 percent rise year-on-year.</p>
<p>Date for four west German states are used to calculate a preliminary figure for Germany as a whole.  </p>
<p>NRW March CPI falls 0.2 pct, up 1.8 pct yr/yr</p>
<p>The statistics office gave the following breakdown of its March cost of living data :</p>
<p>Percentage change</p>
<p>    Index/component			   mth/mth   yr/yr Index</p>
<p>    Overall price index		     -0.2	+1.8  115.3</p>
<p>    Prices exc heating oil, fuel	  -0.1	+1.7  115.2</p>
<p>    Prices exc seasonal goods	     unch	+1.9  115.9</p>
<p>    Prices exc services and repairs     -0.1	+1.4  113.6</p>
<p>    Rents					 +0.2	+3.5  127.4</p>
<p>    Household energy			  -1.7	+2.0  98.6</p>
<p>    Personal goods, services and other  -0.9	+2.6  123.9</p>
<p>    Transport and communications	  +0.2	+0.8  115.2</p>
<p>    Furniture and other household goods +0.1	+0.8  111.4</p>
<p>    Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   -0.2	+0.8  110.0</p>
<p>    Clothing, shoes			   unch	+0.9  112.6</p>
<p>    Health and personal care items	unch	+2.0  115.3</p>
<p>    Education, entertainment, leisure   +0.1	+2.7  112.6</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 REUTER</p>
